{
  "turn_number": 8,
  "player_text": "I slide another coin toward him, slower this time. \"Then sell me one name. Which family, and what debt would make a patrol vanish before their next report?\"",
  "visible_motivation": "The runner says noble family debts sit past the milestone, and that a thicker purse is what buys a careful answer.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want one family name and the debt that could explain the missing patrol.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "\"Names and debts? That's a tough one to pin down,\" the tavern runner replies, voice low and cautious beneath the steady rain. \"Families, sure — old bloodlines like the Durains or the Velmarks have tangled grudges, and their debts? They're not the kind you'd settle at the market. But no honest soul talks openly about who might silence a patrol.\"\n\nHe shifts slightly, eyes flicking toward the gate guards. \"If you want a name, you'd do better to start by shadowing the rumors past the old milestone northwest of the crates. That's where trouble’s been simmering, and that's what some say keeps patrols from sending reports back.\"\n\n\"But be careful—ask too much too loud, and you'd find yourself needing that thick purse to pay for silence.\"",
  "generation_attempt_2": "The tavern runner shakes their head, eyes flickering with a mix of caution and old suspicion. \"I can’t pin it to one family or debt,\" they say, voice low. \"The troubles beyond that milestone are tangled up with many old scores and whispered deals—too many shadows for any one name to hold.\" They glance around briefly. \"If you want names, you’ll need someone with deeper roots and thicker pockets than mine.\"",
