      "model": "gpt-4.1-mini",
      "model_player_facing_text": "\"Names and debts? That's a tough one to pin down,\" the tavern runner replies, voice low and cautious beneath the steady rain. \"Families, sure — old bloodlines like the Durains or the Velmarks have tangled grudges, and their debts? They're not the kind you'd settle at the market. But no honest soul talks openly about who might silence a patrol.\"\n\nHe shifts slightly, eyes flicking toward the gate guards. \"If you want a name, you'd do better to start by shadowing the rumors past the old milestone northwest of the crates. That's where trouble’s been simmering, and that's what some say keeps patrols from sending reports back.\"\n\n\"But be careful—ask too much too loud, and you'd find yourself needing that thick purse to pay for silence.\""
